{"base_rate":0.23622047244094488,"brier":0.10516601049868766,"bss":0.41710564146620843,"bss_hi":0.498039053172138,"bss_lo":0.3327006893308214,"country":"FR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.05234908136482941,"ess":339.2053260992489,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nice</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nice rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>79%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNICE, 7.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.42, ranked 29 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(14&ndash;53) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>363</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>91</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>74%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nice</b> <span class=\"muted\">FR</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.42</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>14&ndash;53\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nice &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nice\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.18747252747252,354.0 99.75260273972603,312.1917808219178 184.49024390243903,213.3170731707317 318.78000000000003,81.09333333333336 409.0046153846154,18.0 409.0046153846154,27.333333333333314 318.78000000000003,149.04 184.49024390243903,288.780487804878 99.75260273972603,362.05479452054794 71.18747252747252,378.1 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"296.01574803149606\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"296.01574803149606\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,372.97520661157023 71.18747252747252,338.0 99.75260273972603,307.2054794520548 184.49024390243903,257.7073170731707 318.78000000000003,115.06666666666666 409.0046153846154,92.66666666666669\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 363 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"372.97520661157023\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 91 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"71.18747252747252\" cy=\"338.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"99.75260273972603\" cy=\"307.2054794520548\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 36%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"184.49024390243903\" cy=\"257.7073170731707\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 74%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"318.78000000000003\" cy=\"115.06666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.0046153846154\" cy=\"92.66666666666669\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(24%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nice the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.53) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.26).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.265</td><td class='num'>10.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>0.312</td><td class='num'>3.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.442</td><td class='num'>5.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.531</td><td class='num'>4.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.70313,"lon":7.26608,"n":762,"n_cities":109,"name":"Nice","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":363,"obs":0.024793388429752067,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03725274725274724,"n":91,"obs":0.12087912087912088,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.11794520547945204,"n":73,"obs":0.2054794520547945,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5740000000000021,"lo":0.2,"mean":0.3573170731707317,"n":82,"obs":0.34146341463414637,"sig":false},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.5740000000000021,"mean":0.7366666666666667,"n":75,"obs":0.7333333333333333,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.9915384615384616,"n":78,"obs":0.7948717948717948,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":7.6,"rank":29,"rank_hi":53.02499999999998,"rank_lo":14.0,"reliability":0.005849331746559678,"resolution":0.080435272693